-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart at a supersingular point: constants and linear parts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{q\ell\}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$; thus $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), with $j\ne 0$. Consider $\mathfrak{X}=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two charts $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ (elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) and $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ (integral over $A[j^{-1}]$). Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ via the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin})$ with image $z$ under $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, such that $y$ is supersingular in the following sense: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ to $\Omega$ with kernel exactly the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point annihilated by $q$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-(X_0X_1^{q}-X_0^{q}X_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v-f\,u)$, subject to two clauses. First, for every $a\in A$ the image of $a$ in the completed stalk (germ at $z$ of the section coming from $\operatorname{Spec}A$) is carried by $e$ to the class of the constant series $C(\sigma a)$. Second, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') H γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — i.e. for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_0,g_0$ of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ and weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g$ giving a nonzero series, every $x\in K$ with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, one has $\iota(\tau x)\cdot q\text{-exp}(g_0\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1})=q\text{-exp}(f_0\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1})$ — and which preserves $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and whose restriction there is the identity modulo the prime $y$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that: $\theta$ transports, through $e$ and the completion map, the action of the restriction of $\tau$ on germs at $z$ of elements of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$; $\theta$ fixes all constants $C(w)$, $w\in W$; for each index $j$ one has $\theta(X_j)-\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\in (X_0,X_1)^2$ in $S$; $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ for all $i,j$, modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ while $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$, then $c\not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem for the two-chart integral model of the modular curve at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: the completed local ring is presented as a Drinfeld chart $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varpi v-fu)$ with $f$ congruent to $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$, with the image of the base ring identified with the constants, and with the level automorphisms acting through linear parts that reduce to scalar multiples of the corresponding elements of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. It feeds the analysis of the quotient of the stalk and the packaging of the Drinfeld chart with its extra equivariance clauses.
